# label: alg:ch68-policy
# pseudocode source: chapters/ch68.tex:62
# caption: Choose a specialization using a conservative finite candidate model.

REQUIRE candidates with established legality, cost intervals, horizon estimate, budget
ENSURE selected candidate satisfies the stated profitability policy
retain the baseline as the default choice
FORALL legal candidates within compilation and memory budgets DO
  compute the worst modeled execution cost over the supplied uncertainty set
  include compilation, recovery, transfer, and retention costs as applicable
  IF modeled total cost improves on baseline by the required margin THEN
    retain the best candidate under the declared objective
  END IF
END FOR
RETURN the selected version or baseline

